window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"nasus","b":"locke","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Nasus"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Wither online — his aggression finally has a tax"},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Purgatory's execute floor — never brawl him at low HP"},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Stacked Q plus Wither out-scales and out-slows him"}],"wants":{"you":["Uninterrupted Q stacks","Wither landed on his engage","Reaching two items intact"],"foe":["Mark chip during your stacking animations","Grinding you low so Silver Stake ramps up","Dodging Wither to keep his mobility"]},"early":"Nothing about this lane is decided early — he chips you with marks while you stack, and that is a trade you happily accept. Farm with Q on cooldown, take Wither at 3 to answer his aggression windows, and do not force fights your kit is simply not built to win at this stage of the game.","mid":"Keep banking stacks through 4-5 and sidestep what poke you can — his chip is annoying, not lethal. Watch Soul Ignition: it damages him first and heals it back at the END of its duration, so Grievous Wounds has to be on him before it expires, not after. At 6 Fury of the Sands survives his all-in, but Purgatory executes.","late":"Two items is where the lane stops being a debate: stacked Siphoning Strike deletes chunks of his health bar and Wither cripples his mobility pattern. Walk him down in the sidelane, but never grind a long fight from low HP — Silver Stake scales with the health you are missing, and Purgatory finishes it.","whys":["You have zero level-1 threat and only want stacks — it is purely a skill stage, so farm clean.","Level 2 is still an even farming lane — you have no kill pattern and he cannot stop you stacking.","At 3 your only real tool is Wither, and he can play around it — the lane stays a skill matchup.","Levels 4-5 remain even — he trades marks into your stacking animations while you tax him with Q whenever he overstays.","Fury of the Sands adds bulk, but Purgatory adds an execute — fights end at his floor.","First item stays even — his poke offsets your early stack lead, so keep farming through the chip.","By two items your stacked Q plus Wither out-scales and out-slows him — the inevitability arrives."]});
