window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"nasus","b":"zaahen","win":["Zaahen","Zaahen","Zaahen","Zaahen","Skill","Nasus","Nasus"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"R bulk blunts his kill threat, but health feeds his E"},{"when":"Wither + 1st tank item","text":"Extended fights come back to even"},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Stacked Q plus Wither wins any prolonged duel"}],"wants":{"you":["Safe stacks under tower","Surviving levels 2-5 without deaths","Grievous Wounds before long duels"],"foe":["Glaive tax on your every CS","Zoning you off stacks early","Filling Determination to revive"]},"early":"Expect to suffer: from level 2 The Darkin Glaive taxes every last-hit and heals him doing it, and by 3 his short trades beat anything you can answer with. Do not fight back — every potion spent on safe stacks is a good deal. Hug tower when zoned, stack what the wave allows, keep deaths at zero.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay his, so treat farming as the victory condition and let him keep the bragging rights. At 6 Fury of the Sands pads your health — but Aureate Rush damages off health, so lean on armour and Grievous Wounds rather than raw HP, since he heals off both the glaive and his ultimate. Then fights come back to even.","late":"This is the whole lane paid off: stacked Siphoning Strike hits like a truck and Wither turns a glaive skirmisher into a slow-motion target. Force long duels in the sidelane — but carry Grievous Wounds, and remember Cultivation of War lets him revive, so the first kill may not stick.","whys":["Level 1 is a neutral farm start — neither of you holds a real combat edge yet.","The Darkin Glaive slashes twice and heals him, so his level-2 poke is free — concede the chip.","At 3 Aureate Rush and glaive spacing win every short trade, and that dash damages off your health, not your armor.","Through 4-5 he still out-duels you and can zone you clean off Siphoning Strike stacks — take only what is safe.","Level 6 evens it, but Fury of the Sands' bonus health also feeds the percent-health damage on Aureate Rush.","By first item your Wither and first tank buy bring extended fights back to level — the tilt finally starts turning your way.","Late, a fully stacked Q plus Wither means you out-scale and beat him in any prolonged duel — inevitability wins."]});
